1
00:07:10,588 --> 00:07:16,588
Based on the incredible true story that inspired Moby Dick

2
00:14:21,176 --> 00:14:27,176
In the Heart of the Sea is a thriller, drama,
adventure film directed by Ron Howard.

3
00:21:31,764 --> 00:21:37,764
In the winter of 1820, the New England whaling ship Essex is assaulted by something no one could
believe—a whale of mammoth size and will, and an almost human sense of vengeance.

4
00:28:42,352 --> 00:28:48,352
Owen Chase, played by Chris Hemsworth.

5
00:35:52,941 --> 00:35:58,941
George Pollard, played by Benjamin Walker.

6
00:43:03,529 --> 00:43:09,529
Matthew Joy, played by Cillian Murphy.

7
00:50:14,117 --> 00:50:20,117
Old Thomas Nickerson, played by Brendan Gleeson.

8
00:57:24,705 --> 00:57:30,705
Herman Melville, played by Ben Whishaw.

9
01:04:35,294 --> 01:04:41,294
Mrs. Nickerson, played by Michelle Fairley.

10
01:11:45,882 --> 01:11:51,882
In the Heart of the Sea is a 2015 historical adventure drama film directed and co-produced by Ron Howard
from a screenplay by Charles Leavitt and a story by Leavitt, Rick Jaffa, and Amanda Silver.

11
01:18:56,470 --> 01:19:02,470
An international co-production between the United States and Spain, the film stars Chris
Hemsworth, Benjamin Walker, Cillian Murphy, Tom Holland, Ben Whishaw, and Brendan Gleeson.

12
01:26:07,058 --> 01:26:13,058
It is based on Nathaniel Philbrick's 2000 non-fiction book In the Heart of the Sea: The Tragedy of the Whaleship Essex, about the
sinking of the American whaling ship Essex in 1820, an event that in part inspired Herman Melville's 1851 novel Moby-Dick.

13
01:33:17,647 --> 01:33:23,647
The film premiered in New York City on December 7, 2015, and was released in
theaters in the United States on December 11, 2015, by Warner Bros.

14
01:40:28,235 --> 01:40:34,235
In the Heart of the Sea received mixed reviews from critics and was a box-office
failure, grossing only $94.3 million against a $100 million budget.

15
01:47:38,823 --> 01:47:44,823
The film explores themes of sea, suicide, ship, ocean, whale.

16
01:54:49,411 --> 01:54:55,411
The tone is emotional and intense.
